course: dictionary
lesson: 2058
title: What happens because of it
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A consequence is something that happens because of an action or event. It is a result. To find it, ask two questions: what did someone do, and what came after? «A punishment like losing screen time is a consequence of what you did, not revenge from your parents.» The punishment comes because of the action, so it is the consequence.
explain: Consequences can be good or bad. «Fights end quickly, but their consequences, like injuries, punishments and lost trust, last much longer.» Here the consequences are bad, and they last longer than the fight. When you meet this word, look for the action it follows and the result that comes next.
explain: In stories, a character can face the consequences of a mistake. In this book, Toad seems to forget about what will happen next: «all fear of obvious consequences … seemed temporarily suspended.» Good readers notice when a character ignores the consequences of their actions.
fact: A consequence is a result: something that happens because of an action or event.
fact: To face the consequences means to accept what happens after you have done something.
fact: "As a consequence" introduces a result, as in "As a consequence, the match was cancelled."
fact: "Of consequence" means important, as in "a matter of consequence".
fact: A cause is what makes something happen, and the consequence is what happens after it.
exercise: «A punishment like losing screen time is a consequence of what you did.» What is a consequence here? | A reward for being kind | Something you lost on purpose | *A result of what you did | A new game to play
exercise: Ellie kicked a ball through a window and had to help pay for a new one. What is the consequence for Ellie? | The window getting bigger | *Having to help pay for a new window | Forgetting about the ball | Getting a prize for football
exercise: What does "of consequence" mean? | Cheap | *Important | Quiet | Early
test: «Fights end quickly, but their consequences … last much longer.» What lasts longer than the fight? | The shouting | Lunch | *The consequences | A tidy room
test: What does "as a consequence" show? | *A result that follows | A colour of paint | A question someone asks | A place to sit down
exam: Which word means something that happens because of an action? | Frantic | Curious | *Consequence | Canopy
